Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(m5-athenak): read AthenaK .bin and .athdf dumps into
 Float32 meshblocks

- change: model/athenak/athenak_mesh.[ch] read "Athena binary output version=1.1" and .athdf mhd_w_bcc dumps into one Float32 array [block][prim][k][j][i] (dens, velx, vely, velz, eint, bcc1-3); press -> eint = Float32(press/(gamma - 1)) with the dump's <mhd>/gamma; temperature dropped; non-finite cells zeroed; parallel pread per block (contiguous .athdf datasets by byte offset, else strided H5Dread)
- change: owning block by the BlackLightPlus meshblock_index paths: dense finest-block table (<= 8e6 cells), else hash on (level, lx1, lx2, lx3) probed coarse to fine, else linear scan; clamped trilinear on cell centres inside the owning block with the BlackLightPlus operation order
- result: s455 (.bin), s122 (.athdf), s093 (.bin, 38.7 GB) load in 0.31 / 0.32 / 3.6 s at 4.0 / 4.0 / 32.0 GB peak RSS (0.89 x file size) [SOLID]
- verify: R06 probe at 1e5 points per snapshot: owning block and all eight interpolated primitives bit-identical to BlackLightPlus sample_primitives
- next: R06 (dag.md)
